format 1
adapter curriculum 1
unit: inside-the-atom

objective u1-atomic-number
statement: Know that the number of protons tells you which element an atom is.
misconception: Elements are made of different kinds of stuff.

item u1-l3-choice-gold-oxygen
type: choice
surfaces: lesson
surfaces: practice
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-ch2

prompt:
    What makes an atom of gold different from an atom of oxygen?

options:
    {"id":"protons","label":"They have different numbers of protons"}
    {"id":"stuff","label":"They are made of different kinds of stuff","note":"Every atom is built from the same three particles. Only the numbers are different."}
    {"id":"solid","label":"Gold atoms are solid and oxygen atoms are hollow","note":"Atoms of every element are mostly empty space."}

answer: protons

explanation:
    Gold atoms have 79 protons and oxygen atoms have 8. The particles are the same kinds. The number of protons is what is different.

item u1-l3-fill-six
type: fill
surfaces: lesson
surfaces: practice
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-ch2

prompt:
    An atom with 6 protons is always ___.

mode: bank

bank:
    {"id":"carbon","label":"carbon"}
    {"id":"nitrogen","label":"nitrogen"}
    {"id":"oxygen","label":"oxygen"}

answer: carbon

explanation:
    6 protons is always carbon. 7 is always nitrogen, and 8 is always oxygen.

item u1-l3-predict-gold-oxygen
type: predict
surfaces: lesson

prompt:
    What is the real difference between an atom of gold and an atom of oxygen?

input: choice

options:
    {"id":"protons","label":"They have different numbers of protons"}
    {"id":"stuff","label":"They are made of different kinds of stuff"}
    {"id":"size","label":"Gold atoms are solid balls and oxygen atoms are hollow"}

answer: protons

explanation:
    Your guess is not scored. Find out as you build.

item u1-x-oxygen-protons
type: choice
surfaces: practice
surfaces: checkpoint
surfaces: review
references: ref-iupac-table

prompt:
    How many protons does every oxygen atom have?

options:
    {"id":"8","label":"8"}
    {"id":"6","label":"6","note":"6 protons would make it carbon."}
    {"id":"7","label":"7","note":"7 protons would make it nitrogen."}

answer: 8

explanation:
    Every oxygen atom has 8 protons.

item u1-x-same-element
type: true_or_myth
surfaces: practice
surfaces: checkpoint
surfaces: review
references: ref-openstax-chem-ch2

statement:
    Two atoms with different numbers of protons can be the same element.

answer: myth

explanation:
    Myth. The number of protons tells you the element. Different numbers of protons mean different elements.
